  "architecture_notes": "The 2D hex CA (champion_rule_perfect) is a synchronous CA with 7-bit neighborhood -> 1-bit center output. It is NOT bit-conserving locally (3->4 bits in the glider) and NOT bijective on the 7-bit state space. The 3D FCC LGCA requires 13-bit -> 13-bit bijective, bit-conserving mappings. These are architecturally incompatible. The hybrid engine resolves this by using synchronous neighbor reads for in-plane channels (ch0-5) instead of LGCA streaming. The inter-plane channels (ch6-11) use standard LGCA stream+identity. This construction GUARANTEES exact reproduction of the 2D hex dynamics on the [111] plane when the in-plane state is computed identically to the 2D case. It is an algebraic identity, not emergence. F3 is triggered because no pure LGCA LUT can simultaneously be bijective, bit-conserving, and match the hex rule - the hex rule inherently changes Hamming weight on the 7-bit subspace."
